Loom AMDGPU: lower f32 fma (scalar.fmaf and vector.fmaf) to the tied VOP2 v_fmac_f32 when the addend dies at the fma,
so the VOPD planner can pair it (v_dual_fmac_f32). Same single rounding as v_fma_f32 (bit-identical results). A splat
addend keeps the VOP3 form: its lanes are copies of one scalar that the allocator may place in one register, which the
tied form would overwrite for the remaining lanes (kv8 decode attention's dequant). The yah iu4 GEMM fold
(acc = fma(f32(c), scale, acc)) goes from 64 VOP3 fma to 34 dual + 3 single fmac per phase: 31 fewer VALU issue slots,
pp2048 GEMM cycles -0.5%.
